      "text_raw": "A better sketch of the peak-\ning in the frequency domain\n(or in the Bode diagram) is\nshown in this slide.\nThe value of the maxi-\nmum peaking P is given as\nf\nwell. It is clear that for a\ndamping f of 0.7, we obtain\na maximally-flat response.\nGoing to larger f reduces\nthe bandwidth too much.\nAlso, going to smaller\nvalues of f causes peaking\nindeed.\nFor zero f, we would have\na peak to infinity, which is\ntypical for an oscillator.",
      "text": "A better sketch of the peaking in the frequency domain (or in the Bode diagram) is shown in this slide. The value of the maximum peaking P is given as f well. It is clear that for a damping f of 0.7, we obtain a maximally-flat response. Going to larger f reduces the bandwidth too much. Also, going to smaller values of f causes peaking indeed. For zero f, we would have a peak to infinity, which is typical for an oscillator."
    }
